; NextDAAD XBN extern support Task 1 fixture - EXTERN/CALL/#int probe.
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run; staged as the active
; GAME.DDB in sd\XBN\ by tests\build-tests.ps1 -Xbn, which also stages
; the fixture extern binary tests\xbn\xbntest.asm assembles to
; tests\out\xbn\GAME.XBN as GAME.XBN in that same folder (-XbnNoBin
; omits it entirely for the XABS/no-XBN control; -XbnBad <kind> stages
; a corrupt-header/truncated variant instead, for Task 2). Skeleton
; (CTL/VOC/STX/MTX/OTX/LTX/CON/OBJ/PRO shape, required system message
; block) follows tests\gmodegate.dsf.
;
; WHAT IT PINS
; Task 1 is scaffolding only - these verbs assert the EXTERN/CALL/#int
; CONTRACT xbn.inc documents, not any interpreter behaviour: zero
; interpreter source changes land until Task 2+, so every one of these
; checks is EXPECTED TO FAIL (or no-op) until then.
;   XREG - the register contract EXTERN hands the extern on entry:
;          A=B=param1, C=fn, HL=flags+param1, DE=objTable+param1*6,
;          IX=flags base ($A200). xbntest.asm's ext_main echoes each of
;          those into flags 200-205 for this entry to PRINT back.
;   XCAL - a direct CALL into a staged XBN reaches the intended
;          address (xbntest.asm's call_target, which sets flag 220).
;   XCNR - negative control: CALL to an address outside the mapped XBN
;          window ($8000, well below XBN_ORG) must no-op, not crash.
;   XTIK - the #int hook (xbntest.asm's int_tick) increments a flag
;          every frame while an XBN is staged.
;   XSVC - the service probe entry (fn 21); Task 6 fills flags 206+
;          once the service jump table exists.
;   XABS - the no-XBN control: with NO GAME.XBN staged (-XbnNoBin),
;          EXTERN must stay inert and flag 200 must stay at the CLEARed
;          0, never the 9 a staged XBN would echo.
;   XFIO - the file-service probe (fn 22, xbntest.asm's fio_probe):
;          SVC_FOPEN/FWRITE/FCLOSE then SVC_FOPEN/FREAD/FCLOSE round-trip
;          8 bytes through XBNFIO.TMP on the card and compares them.
;   XMSG - the GETMSG probe (fn 23, xbntest.asm's msg_probe): decodes
;          MTX message 0 into savStage, echoes its first byte and
;          length, then re-prints it through a bounded SVC_PUTCHAR
;          loop; fn 24 (msg_probe_bad) then checks the out-of-range
;          error path (message 50, past the DDB's single MTX entry).
;
; MTX message 0 is reserved verbatim as the Task 8 SVC_GETMSG probe
; payload ("TICKER MESSAGE FOR GETMSG") - never printed as a boot
; banner, so a later task can read it back through the service call
; and compare bytes rather than screen text. Task 9's shipped ticker
; worked example (authoring-kit\externs\ticker\ticker.asm) consumes
; the same message 0 through the same service call.
;   XTCK - drives the Task 9 ticker example (EXTERN 0 30 arms it on
;          message 0, EXTERN 0 31 disarms it). This verb does not
;          reach xbntest.asm at all - -XbnTicker (tests\build-tests.ps1)
;          stages the ticker's own GAME.XBN in place of the fixture, so
;          this entry is only meaningful in that combination; against
;          the plain fixture XBN, fn 30/31 fall through xbntest.asm's
;          ext_main unrecognised and no-op.

#define fPlayer  38

/CTL
_
/VOC
XREG   100 verb
XCAL   101 verb
XCNR   102 verb
XTIK   103 verb
XSVC   104 verb
XFIO   105 verb
XMSG   106 verb
XABS   107 verb
XTCK   108 verb
XFAD   109 verb
XFDI   110 verb
XMS6   111 verb
XGFB   112 verb
XFSC   113 verb
XFSO   114 verb
XDRK   115 verb
XRST   116 verb
XRLD   117 verb
XDCL   118 verb
XARM   119 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "TICKER MESSAGE FOR GETMSG"
; Messages 1-6: the SVC_GETMSG multi-fetch regression corpus (the
; svc-getmsg HL-clobber defect, found 2026-08-15 in the field). Heavy
; shared phrasing FORCES DRC to token-compress them - the defect only
; fires on token references, which is exactly why the original
; single-message fixture never caught it. xbntest.asm's msg_multi
; (fn 25) fetches all six in one EXTERN and checks each length and
; first two characters against MSGTAB - if these texts change, that
; table changes with them, and the tokenisation byte-check in the
; harness must still hold (raw bytes < decoded length).
/1 "Northern lights over the northern mountains tonight"
/2 "Southern lights over the southern mountains tonight"
/3 "Eastern winds over the eastern mountains this evening"
/4 "Western winds over the western mountains this evening"
/5 "Midnight bells over the midnight mountains ring softly"
/6 "Morning bells over the morning mountains ring softly"
/OTX
/0 "a spare widget"
/LTX
/0 "The XBN test arena."
/CON
/0
/OBJ
;obj  starts  weight    c w  5 4 3 2 1 0 9 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 0    noun   adjective
/0    0   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
; ---- main location loop (template shape, no graphics - see
; tests\gmodegate.dsf for the gated version this is trimmed from) ----
> _ _   AT 0                    ; starting the game?
        PROCESS 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        CLS
        DESC @fPlayer
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
; ---- parser loop (template shape, trimmed) ----
; The PROCESS 5 dispatch below is LOAD-BEARING: this fixture was first
; shipped without it (copied from gmodegate.dsf's skeleton, which has no
; command decoder at all - its checks run at boot from PRO 6), so every
; typed verb fell through MOVE to SYSMESS 8 "I can't do that". The X*
; verbs only reach PRO 5 through this entry (test.dsf's template shape).
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 5
        ISDONE
        REDO
> _ _   MOVE fPlayer
        CLS
        RESTART
> _ _   NEWTEXT
        LT 33 14
        SYSMESS 7
        REDO
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        REDO
/PRO 5
; ---- command decoder: one entry per XBN probe verb ----
> XREG _   LET 150 42        ; park a known value where the echo can see it
           LET 33 0          ; not required; keeps entry shape uniform
           EXTERN 42 20      ; forwarded fn 20 -> echo (param1=42)
           PRINT 200         ; expect 42
           PRINT 201         ; expect 20
           PRINT 204         ; expect 162 ($A2)
           PRINT 205         ; expect 0
           DONE
> XCAL _   CALL 113 192       ; COUPLED to tests\xbn\xbntest.asm's call_target
                             ; label, address $C071 (lsb 113, msb 192) - read
                             ; from tests\out\xbn\xbntest.sym after assembly
                             ; (sjasmplus --sym); re-encode here if xbntest.asm
                             ; changes and call_target's address moves.
           PRINT 220         ; expect 119 ($77)
           CALL 142 226       ; Task 4's owed check: tail_marker, address
                             ; $E28E (lsb 142, msb 226) - the SECOND 8K page
                             ; of the XBN window, proving CALL dispatch
                             ; reaches page 2 and not only page 1. Same
                             ; re-encode caveat as call_target above.
           PRINT 222         ; expect 153 ($99)
           DONE
> XCNR _   CLEAR 220
           CALL 0 128        ; $8000 - out of window, must no-op
           PRINT 220         ; expect 0
           DONE
> XTIK _   CLEAR 221
           PAUSE 100         ; one second. DRC HALVES every PAUSE
                             ; operand for the NEXTDAAD target at
                             ; compile time (drb.php getDurationAdjustment:
                             ; baseLength 100 / DEFAULT_NOTE_DURATION 200),
                             ; so this ships as operand 50 = 50 frames.
                             ; An authored PAUSE 50 shipped as 25 and made
                             ; the original "expect ~50" unmeetable - 25
                             ; was the CORRECT reading (silicon-confirmed
                             ; 2026-08-14, 25 ticks in 25 frames = 1:1).
           PRINT 221         ; expect 48-52 (50 +- ISR jitter)
           DONE
> XSVC _   EXTERN 0 21       ; service probe fn - Task 6 fills flags 206+
           PRINT 206
           PRINT 207
           DONE
> XFIO _   EXTERN 0 22        ; fio_probe: write/close/reopen/read/compare
           PRINT 208         ; expect 1
           DONE
> XMSG _   EXTERN 0 23        ; msg_probe: SVC_GETMSG on MTX message 0
           PRINT 210         ; expect 84 ('T')
           PRINT 211         ; expect 1
           EXTERN 0 24        ; msg_probe_bad: out-of-range message number
           PRINT 212         ; expect 1
           DONE
> XABS _   CLEAR 200
           EXTERN 9 20       ; with NO XBN staged this must stay inert
           PRINT 200         ; expect 0 in the no-XBN leg, 9 with XBN
           DONE
> XTCK _   EXTERN 0 30       ; Task 9 ticker example: arm on message 0
           PAUSE 100         ; ships as operand 50 = ONE second (DRC
                             ; halves PAUSE for this target, see XTIK
                             ; above) - message ticks out in ~0.5s, the
                             ; rest is settle time before the DONE
           EXTERN 0 31       ; disarm (idempotent - int_tick already
                             ; disarms itself once the message is fully
                             ; ticked out)
           DONE
> XFAD _   PICTURE 1         ; only meaningful with -XbnFade staged
           DISPLAY 0         ; (fade example as GAME.XBN + 001.NX2 art);
                             ; without art PICTURE skips DISPLAY, and
                             ; without the fade XBN fn 40 no-ops
           LET 241 0         ; fade speed: default (about one second)
           CLEAR 240         ; completion flag
           EXTERN 224 40     ; fade out to red (%11100000) - a colour,
                             ; not black, so a successful fade cannot be
                             ; mistaken for a blanked screen
           PAUSE 150         ; ships as 75 frames (DRC halves PAUSE) -
                             ; fade is 8 steps x 6 frames + snapshot
           PRINT 240         ; expect 1 (hook set it at completion)
           DONE
> XFDI _   CLEAR 240
           EXTERN 0 41       ; fade back in to the snapshot
           PAUSE 150
           PRINT 240         ; expect 1
           DONE
> XMS6 _   EXTERN 0 25       ; msg_multi: six token-compressed fetches
                             ; in ONE call (the svc-getmsg HL-clobber
                             ; regression - the defect corrupted the
                             ; DDB token table from the first token
                             ; reference of the second fetch)
           PRINT 213         ; expect 6 (messages verified)
           SYSMESS 16        ; "Press any key." - printed AFTER the
                             ; fetches so DDB/token-table health is
                             ; visible on screen: the defect garbled
                             ; exactly this kind of later print
           DONE
> XGFB _   PICTURE 1         ; plain buffered reveal - no fade anywhere
           GFX 0 4           ; graphics to buffer (AFTER the PICTURE
                             ; condition - the ratified ordering)
           DISPLAY 0         ; must NOT appear yet
           PAUSE 100         ; ships as 50 frames - a visible hold in
                             ; which the screen must stay unchanged
           GFX 0 2           ; picture appears NOW, correct colours
           GFX 0 3
           DONE
> XFSC _   PICTURE 1         ; scene change through a fade, NEW sequence
           DISPLAY 0         ; picture 1 up at full brightness
           LET 241 0         ; default fade speed
           CLEAR 240
           EXTERN 224 40     ; fade out to red (%11100000)
           EXTERN 0 43
           PICTURE 2         ; condition - aborts on missing art (screen
                             ; then stays solid red: recover with XFDI)
           GFX 0 4
           DISPLAY 0
           EXTERN 0 42
           GFX 0 2
           GFX 0 3
           EXTERN 0 41
           EXTERN 0 43
           PRINT 240         ; expect 1
           DONE
> XFSO _   PICTURE 1         ; OLD sequence - regression leg, band and all
           DISPLAY 0
           LET 241 0
           CLEAR 240
           EXTERN 224 40
           EXTERN 0 43
           PICTURE 2
           DISPLAY 0
           EXTERN 0 42
           EXTERN 0 41
           EXTERN 0 43
           PRINT 240
           DONE
> XDRK _   EXTERN 224 40     ; darkness abort: fade out first
           EXTERN 0 43
           PICTURE 99        ; no 099 art staged: condition FAILS, the
           GFX 0 4           ; entry aborts HERE - GFX 0 4 never runs
           DISPLAY 0
> XDRK _   EXTERN 0 41       ; second entry: recover - fade back in
           EXTERN 0 43
           DONE              ; then type XFAD: picture must appear
                             ; (draw target was never set)
> XRST _   GFX 0 4           ; arm buffer mode, then RESTART must clear
           RESTART           ; it - then type XFAD: picture must appear
> XRLD _   RAMSAVE           ; snapshot, arm buffer mode, restore -
           GFX 0 4           ; RAMLOAD must clear the mode - then type
           RAMLOAD 255       ; XFAD: picture must appear
           DONE
> XDCL _   PICTURE 1         ; DISPLAY 1 in both modes (spec 9.7)
           GFX 0 4
           DISPLAY 0         ; deferred
           DISPLAY 1         ; buffer mode: clears the BACK surface (the
                             ; staged pixels) - screen must NOT change
           PAUSE 100
           GFX 0 3           ; mode off; the deferral is still pending
           DISPLAY 1         ; screen mode: clear-flip - transparent
                             ; picture area, NO garbage rows, pending
                             ; reveal discarded
           DONE              ; then XFAD: picture appears normally
> XARM _   GFX 0 4           ; arm buffer mode and stop - the manual
           DONE              ; SAVE/LOAD reset check drives this
/PRO 6
; ---- one-shot init ----
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        PAPER 0
        INK 7
        CLS
        MES "NEXTDAAD XBN EXTERN FIXTURE#n"
/END
